{"name":"Sappanwood","hex":"#9e3d3f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sappanwood","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Wood of Biancaea sappan (syn. Caesalpinia sappan), a flowering timber tree of the legume family Fabaceae that also yields medicine and red dye."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sappanwood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Biancaea sappan","blocks":[{"text":"Biancaea sappan is a species of flowering tree in the legume family, Fabaceae, that is native to tropical Asia. Common names in English include sappan, sappanwood and Indian redwood. It was previously ascribed to the genus Caesalpinia. Sappanwood is related to brazilwood, and was itself called brasilwood in the Middle Ages."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Caesalpinia_sappan1.jpg/330px-Caesalpinia_sappan1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biancaea_sappan","wikidata":"Q56088062"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Biancaea_sappan_leaves_flower_buds.jpg/120px-Biancaea_sappan_leaves_flower_buds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Biancaea_sappan_leaves_flower_buds.jpg/250px-Biancaea_sappan_leaves_flower_buds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Biancaea_sappan_leaves_flower_buds.jpg/120px-Biancaea_sappan_leaves_flower_buds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABiancaea_sappan_leaves_flower_buds.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Biancaea_sappan_fruits.jpg/120px-Biancaea_sappan_fruits.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikim